Scenario:
A banking application has multiple development teams. Every code change needs to go through automated build, testing, code-quality checks, security scanning, containerization and controlled deployment before reaching the production environment.

Secure CI/CD Pipeline for Banking Application
Overview:
This project demonstrates a production-oriented Secure CI/CD pipeline for a sample banking application.
The objective is to automate the application delivery lifecycle while integrating security and quality checks into the CI/CD process.
The implementation is based on a generic banking application scenario and does not use any real customer, organization, production, or confidential data.
Consideration: 
Consider a banking application that provides services such as:
	Customer login
	Account information
	Fund transfer
	Transaction history
	Payment processing
	Customer profile management
Multiple developers continuously contribute code to the application.
The organization wants a CI/CD process where every code change is:

1-Version controlled
2-Automatically built
3-Unit tested
4-Checked for code quality
5-Scanned for security vulnerabilities
6-Packaged as a Docker image
7-Scanned for container vulnerabilities
8-Stored in a container registry
9-Deployed automatically to a non-production environment
10-Promoted to production only after required validations and approvals

